      ],
      "text": "**If you’re healthy and just going out briefly, a mask isn’t necessarily needed—but avoid strenuous or prolonged outdoor activity tonight.** Singapore’s 24-hour PSI forecast for **Saturday, October 17** is **150–230 (Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy)**; NEA’s latest reported 1-hour PM2.5 range was **44–148** at 8 p.m., varying by area. Check your local reading before heading out. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))\n\nIf you’re elderly, pregnant, a child, or have heart or lung disease, **minimise outdoor time**; if you must be outside for a while, an **N95** may help reduce exposure. NEA says healthy people generally don’t need one for a short commute. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))",
